  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 138 AM EDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\n*** TURNING GRADUALLY MILDER MIDWEEK ***\n\nAs gentle northerly flow continues, the local area will feel \nprogressively drier and less warm Monday night into Tuesday, by \nwhich time dewpoints should dip into the 50s across northern \nportions of the area. Parts of southern Kentucky may still warm into \nthe 80s Tuesday afternoon, but most locations will see highs in the \n70s and overnight lows in the upper 50s to low 60s. Wednesday and \nonward, the continual northerly flow should (NBM chances are\nroughly 60-80%) maintain highs in the 70s and lows in the 50s \neach day area wide - which, though much cooler than what we've \nbecome accustomed to as of late, is near normal for late \nSeptember.",
